    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived `timezone` field to the owner response, sourced from the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n- **`util/RegionTimezone.java`** (new): a small, single-responsibility pinned lookup `region \u2192 IANA name` (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane), returning `null` for `null`/unknown regions. This mirrors the existing sibling tables (`CityRegion`, `RegionPostcodes`).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**: added a `timezone(owner)` default method that derives the timezone from the owner's already-computed `locality(owner)` (the region), plus the `@Mapping(target = \"timezone\", ...)` entry and the import. It reuses the existing locality derivation rather than re-deriving the region.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`**: declared the read-only `timezone` string property on the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, including the new `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`) is green.",
